<header class="hero"><p class="eyebrow">HUMAN GOLD RUSH LESSON</p><h1>Community Force</h1><p class="intro">A pledge names a future intention. Trust makes coordinated action possible; fulfillment places that force into motion.</p><blockquote>How can a community recognize trade value without turning gratitude into money?</blockquote></header><aside class="notice"><strong>Important distinction</strong><p>$102 is the MEGAvoter pledge bundle ($12 membership + $30 Tiger’s Eye + $60 Organized Krill Kit). $103 is the community value represented by ten $10.30 allocations. They are separate measures.</p></aside><section class="content-grid"><article><span>01</span><div><h2>Seeking Gratitude</h2><p>A product, service, contribution, or act may be recognized with gratitude. That recognition is not accepted as money, payment, credit, stored value, or a financial claim.</p></div></article><article><span>02</span><div><h2>Need money? Select YAM-is-On</h2><p>A MEGAvoter merchant, vendor, or seller places a YAM-is-ON hang tag or sticker on a product or service offered for $30 through the YAM JAM payment rail. The seller collects the revenue and accepts responsibility for the $10.30 community allocation recorded for quarterly settlement.</p></div></article><article><span>03</span><div><h2>If not, select community surplus</h2><p>If no money is accepted, the seller, sponsor, or messenger uses Seeking Gratitude. The same $30 allocation pattern is issued only as XP Experience Presence. It can never become payment, remuneration, stored value, or a financial claim.</p></div></article><article><span>04</span><div><h2>YAM JAM</h2><p>YAM JAM is the payment rail used by the MEGAvoter seller for the $30 sale. The XP General Ledger does not hold the money; it preserves the seller’s VFN testament, two-device delivery evidence, maturity, dispute, settlement, and extinguishment status.</p></div></article><article><span>05</span><div><h2>The clear distinction</h2><p>Seeking Gratitude measures service without money. YAM-is-ON documents a $30 sale through YAM JAM. Both become comparable behavioral evidence through the XP append-only General Ledger.</p></div></article><article><span>06</span><div><h2>Pledge tiers, not price tags</h2><p>MEGAvoter onboarding records a $12 annual membership pledge. Eligible members may separately reserve the $30 Tiger’s Eye touchstone and the $60 Organized Krill Kit, creating the $102 pledge bundle when all three are selected. A pledge or $0 backorder is not itself a completed sale.</p></div></article><article><span>07</span><div><h2>Ten-packs in circulation</h2><p>The initial Organized Krill Kit contains ten hang tags or stickers. Additional YAM-is-ON or Seeking Gratitude issuance is authorized only after at least 51% of the current lot receives a valid two-device delivery response. A 10-pack therefore requires six valid responses before reissuance.</p></div></article><article><span>08</span><div><h2>Time is the actual scarcity</h2><p>Organized Krill turns XP (Experience Presence) into a way of producing Human Gold: no one gets more than 24 hours in a day, and that limit — not a price — is the most important factor in describing what it means to show up.</p></div></article><article><span>09</span><div><h2>From your seat: the $4 line</h2><p>For each confirmed $30 YAM-is-ON sale, the seller records $10 COGS, $9.70 seller margin, and $10.30 community value: $5 buyer rebate, $4 social impact, $1 patronage, and $0.30 proof of delivery. Seeking Gratitude mirrors those allocations only in XP.</p></div></article></section><section class="media-section"><div class="section-heading"><p>MEDIA FOR THIS LESSON</p><h2>Watch, listen, and discuss</h2></div><div class="media-grid"><article class="media-card video"><div class="media-frame"><span>▶</span><small>VIDEO 1</small></div><h3>Community Force: orientation</h3><p>Reserved for the featured story or introductory video.</p><a href="#">Transcript coming soon</a></article><article class="media-card video"><div class="media-frame"><span>▶</span><small>VIDEO 2</small></div><h3>Community conversation</h3><p>Reserved for a demonstration, conversation, or local example.</p><a href="#">Discussion guide coming soon</a></article><article class="media-card podcast"><div class="media-frame"><span>◉</span><small>PODCAST</small></div><h3>Listen and reflect</h3><p>Reserved for the facilitator or community podcast episode.</p><a href="#">Transcript coming soon</a></article></div></section><section class="content-grid"><article><span>11</span><div><h2>Seller as VFN</h2><p>The MEGAvoter seller acts as the Voluntary Fulfillment Network for vouchers they issue. On the last day of each month, the seller posts a testament of issued, pending, matured, disputed, and extinguished obligations to the XP append-only General Ledger.</p></div></article><article><span>12</span><div><h2>Monthly testimony, quarterly settlement</h2><p>Monthly postings preserve the fiat-economy record. Settlement occurs only at the applicable twelve-week quarterly close so the YAM-is-ON record can be compared with the complete Seeking Gratitude Presence dataset.</p></div></article></section>
